1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Hollywood Leading Men — Then & Now

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,840
Welcome to Hollywood Leading Men, Then and Now.

3
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:16,678
We begin with Tom Cruise.

4
00:00:16,778 --> 00:00:23,294
A nineteen eighty nine Oscars portrait catches him
just after Top Gun made him a defining movie star.

5
00:00:23,394 --> 00:00:29,909
A recent festival image shows the same focused
screen presence, now backed by decades of daring
action films.

6
00:00:30,009 --> 00:00:37,260
Leonardo DiCaprio moved from youthful dramatic
roles to an Oscar winning career that includes
Titanic, The Departed, and The Revenant.

7
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:42,773
His two portraits trace a performer who keeps
choosing ambitious collaborators and very different
worlds.

8
00:00:42,873 --> 00:00:45,346
Tom Hanks brings another kind of range.

9
00:00:45,446 --> 00:00:53,432
From the playful energy of Big to the humanity of
Forrest Gump, Apollo 13, and Toy Story, he made
warmth feel cinematic.

10
00:00:53,532 --> 00:00:59,780
Look closely at these first three pairs, then see
which familiar expression has stayed with each
actor.

11
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,678
Now for three more leading men.

12
00:01:05,778 --> 00:01:14,409
Brad Pitt arrived with a restless edge that carried
from Thelma and Louise to Fight Club and Once Upon
a Time in Hollywood.

13
00:01:14,509 --> 00:01:19,345
The years change the style, but the calm intensity
remains easy to recognize.

14
00:01:19,445 --> 00:01:25,799
Denzel Washington has brought authority and detail
to characters in Glory, Malcolm X, Training Day,
and Fences.

15
00:01:25,899 --> 00:01:30,354
His portraits frame a career built on listening as
carefully as speaking.

16
00:01:30,454 --> 00:01:39,465
George Clooney turned television charm into a
varied film career, from Ocean's Eleven to Syriana,
The Descendants, and directing work behind the
camera.

17
00:01:39,565 --> 00:01:42,123
Six careers, six different paths through Hollywood.

18
00:01:42,223 --> 00:01:45,260
Which early and recent pairing surprised you most?

19
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The close-up chapter begins. Look again at the portraits, the years, and the roles.

20
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:31,600
Which early and later pairing surprised you most?

21
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:59,600
